{#
  LLM Vision per-model pricing table — THE single place rates are defined.
  Place at: /config/custom_templates/llmvision_rates.jinja
  Reload after editing: Developer Tools -> YAML -> "Custom Jinja2 templates"
  (service: homeassistant.reload_custom_templates). No restart needed.

  Returns "input_rate,output_rate,source" (USD per million tokens):
    source = "table"    -> model has an explicit entry below
    source = "fallback" -> model unknown; priced at the default helpers, and
                           the "unknown model" automation raises a notification

  Conventions:
  - claude-sonnet-5 (the primary model) deliberately references the two
    input_number helpers instead of literals, so the scheduled 2026-09-01
    rate-change automation (which updates the helpers) flows through here
    automatically. Other models are literals: edit this file, then reload.
  - Keyed by model only. If a provider is ever added where the SAME model id
    has different pricing (e.g. OpenRouter vs OpenAI direct), the key must
    become provider|model — the llm_provider attribute is already in every
    ledger row to support that split.
  - Matching is LONGEST PREFIX, not exact: providers report dated variants
    ('claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', 'gpt-4o-2024-08-06') that price the same
    as the base model. Longest-prefix means a more specific key (e.g. a
    differently-priced '-mini' variant) can be added later and win over the
    base entry. Discovered 2026-08-16: a dated Haiku id fell through exact
    matching to fallback and one ledger row overpriced at 2/10 instead of
    1/5 (disclosed, not corrected).
  - Rates below verified 2026-08-16 (Anthropic list prices). Do not add
    models from memory — check the provider's pricing page first; a wrong
    rate here is stamped into ledger rows permanently.
#}
{%- macro rates(model) -%}
{%- set fb = (states('input_number.llm_vision_rate_input_per_mtok') | float(0) | string)
     ~ ',' ~ (states('input_number.llm_vision_rate_output_per_mtok') | float(0) | string) -%}
{%- set table = {
  'claude-sonnet-5': fb ~ ',table',
  'claude-haiku-4-5': '1.00,5.00,table',
  'claude-opus-5': '5.00,25.00,table'
} -%}
{%- set hit = namespace(val=none, klen=0) -%}
{%- for k, v in table.items() -%}
  {%- if model.startswith(k) and (k | length) > hit.klen -%}
    {%- set hit.val = v -%}
    {%- set hit.klen = k | length -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- hit.val if hit.val is not none else fb ~ ',fallback' -}}
{%- endmacro -%}
